comments.text:
Direct integration review rejected the first synthetic-only selector because the production projection includes every evidence row in priorities and every score in optimization outcomes as not_run. That would have preserved the full artifact fanout despite passing tests.

Correction:
- priority briefs are limited by the explicit stakeholder display cutoff;
- empty and not_run outcomes do not create briefs;
- score-specific questions/issues and material optimizer outcomes do;
- stable hashed score_ref metadata now flows through portfolio, priority, feedback-investment, issue, and outcome rows so duplicate display names remain distinguishable without exposing raw opaque IDs.

Two disjoint Terra Coding Agent tasks implemented these changes after failing outside-in specifications. Main-agent review inspected both diffs. The complete optimization namespace now passes 406 tests with one existing deprecation warning, and git diff validation passes. The baseline run remains on pre-fix loaded code and continues to quantify repeated publication delay.
